        84.959980000000002,
        517.65974479999988,
        425.12669493662725,
        11.979110399999968
      ],
      "text" : "Converting between standard notation and scientific notation is important to"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        84.959979999999973,
        503.13944479999981,
        425.18582631421441,
        11.979110400000025
      ],
      "text" : "understand how scientific notation works and what it does. Here our main"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        84.959979999999973,
        488.49964479999983,
        425.24727610841597,
        11.979110400000025
      ],
      "text" : "interest is to be able to multiply and divide numbers in scientific notation using"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        84.959979999999973,
        473.97974479999982,
        425.15748308728325,
        11.979110400000025
      ],
      "text" : "exponent properties. The way we do this is first do the operation with the front"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        84.959979999999973,
        459.33954479999983,
        425.17371160445441,
        11.979110400000025
      ],
      "text" : "number (multiply or divide) then use exponent properties to simplify the 10’s."
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        84.959979999999973,
        444.81964479999982,
        425.21855839050249,
        11.979110400000025
      ],
      "text" : "Scientific notation is the only time where it will be allowed to have negative expo-"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        84.959979999999973,
        430.29974479999981,
        425.2010767171073,
        11.979110400000025
      ],
      "text" : "nents in our final solution. The negative exponent simply informs us that we are"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 11.955200000000001,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        84.959979999999973,
        415.65994479999983,
        318.731902675968,
        11.979110400000025
      ],
      "text" : "dealing with small numbers. Consider the following examples."
